# Install GR-DOS on a blank 20 MB disk (615 cylinders, 4 heads, 17
# sectors) from the 1.44 MB release image: FDISK makes a Primary DOS
# Partition of all of it, active, and restarts the machine; FORMAT C: and
# SYS C: make it a system disk, and COMMAND.COM is copied to it. With the
# floppy ejected, the machine boots from the hard disk. FORMAT gives the
# partition of fewer than 65,536 sectors type 04h.
disk 21411840 615/4/17
expect table
wait A:\\>
type FDISK
key ret
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
wait Enter choice
key 1 ret
wait make the partition active
key ret
wait System will now restart
key spc
wait A:\\>
type FORMAT C:
key ret
wait Proceed with Format \(Y/N\)\?
key y ret
wait Volume label \(11 characters, ENTER for none\)\?
type GRDOS
key ret
wait 21309440 bytes total disk space\n +21309440 bytes available on disk\n\n +2048 bytes in each allocation unit(?s:.*)A:\\>
type SYS C:
key ret
wait System transferred(?s:.*)A:\\>
type COPY COMMAND.COM C:\
key ret
wait 1 File\(s\) copied(?s:.*)A:\\>
eject
reset
wait Enter new date
key ret
wait Enter new time
key ret
wait \nC>
type VER
key ret
wait GR-DOS Version 4\.00\n+C>
type DIR
key ret
wait Volume in drive C is GRDOS(?s:.*)COMMAND +COM +\d+(?s:.*)1 File\(s\) +\d+ bytes free\n+C>
quit
